  <diagram id="ppGJttjt45pB7GuRdLLa" name="3-Questions-Assumptions">
    <mxGraphModel grid="1" page="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="0guOXwWDXlD0LigR_Erw-2" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 220%;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;QUESTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. (7.1) Who is the regional director and is he stored as an employee?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. (7.2) What is the passing score of a course?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. (7.3) Does the special price of a luxury car change over time?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. (7.3) Can two rates of the same category overlap?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. (7.7) Must the customer email be unique?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. (7.7) Can a blacklist be removed later?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. (7.7) Does the blacklist also block walk-in rentals?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8. (7.10) How many points does a rental give, and do points expire?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. (7.11) Must the rented car be from the reserved category?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;10. (7.12) Who are the additional drivers?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;11. (7.13) Do extras and insurance prices need their own history?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;12. (7.16) How is a monthly invoice related to payments, and are refunds allowed?&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="520" width="1030" x="-700" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="0guOXwWDXlD0LigR_Erw-6" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 220%;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;ASSUMPTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. (all) Every entity table has a surrogate key named ID. SRS numbers and codes stay as NN UQ columns.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. (all) Weak entities and M:N tables use a composite primary key without ID.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. (all) Age, tier, points balance, promo uses and current branch are calculated, not stored.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. (7.1) The branch address is split into street, city and governorate.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. (7.1) Is24Hours is added for branches that work 24 hours.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;6. (7.1) The 21 years rule is checked at hire date.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;7. (7.1) The manager is stored in BRANCH because every branch must have one.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;8. (7.2) Each training attempt is one row in ENROLLMENT.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;9. (7.3) A category rate is identified by category and start date. An empty end date means it is still valid.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;10. (7.3) The special price of a vehicle is an optional column.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;11. (7.3) Every status change is saved in STATUS_LOG.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;12. (7.3) The current branch of a vehicle comes from its last transfer.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;13. (7.5) A GPS device in the warehouse has no vehicle.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;14. (7.7) Every customer is Individual or Corporate, never both.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;15. (7.7) An individual has either a national ID or a passport number.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;16. (7.7) Customer email is required but not unique.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;17. (7.7) A customer has one blacklist at most, stored in CUSTOMER.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;18. (7.10) Points are always positive and Type says earned or redeemed.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;19. (7.12) A reservation becomes one rental at most. A walk-in has no reservation.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;20. (7.12) An extension is a new rental that points to the old one.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;21. (7.12) The main driver is empty for individual customers.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;22. (7.4, 7.13) Extras and insurance prices are saved on the rental.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;23. (7.16) Invoice is a new entity for corporate monthly billing.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;24. (7.16) The bank reference is empty for cash and unique for card and bank.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;25. (7.14) A damage report is identified by the rental and the report number.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;26. (7.15) The total cost of a job card is stored.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1000" width="1230" x="-730" y="640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="0guOXwWDXlD0LigR_Erw-7" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div style=&quot;line-height: 220%;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;CONTRADICTIONS&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Section 7.7 says authorized drivers are known only through their company. Section 8 says a driver can also be an individual customer.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. Section 7.16 says a rental can have several payments. The Finance note says corporate clients get one monthly invoice.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. Section 7.3 says prices are set per category. The COO note says some luxury cars have their own price.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 20px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. Section 7.1 says a manager runs only one branch. It also says the regional director replaces a resigned manager maybe in several branches.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="320" width="1500" x="-720" y="1640" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
